# Profile: large. A Docker VM of 16 GB or more, for 500k to 1M events without
# the 6 GB ceilings deciding the outcome. Ceilings sum to about 14.4 GB, which
# leaves roughly 1.5 GB of a 16 GB VM for the Docker daemon.
#
# Applied to .env by `make profile PROFILE=large`. Run `make preflight` after
# applying it: it compares these ceilings with the VM's real memory.
#
# S3_GOMEMLIMIT stays about 512 MiB under MEM_S3 so the Go GC works to stay
# inside the cgroup; the gap covers memory the GC cannot see (docs/adr/0003).
MEM_KAFKA=1536m
MEM_KAFKA_HEAP="-Xmx768m -Xms768m"
MEM_POSTGRES=512m
MEM_CLICKHOUSE=3072m
MEM_REDIS=64m
MEM_S3=2048m
S3_GOMEMLIMIT=1536MiB
MEM_AIRFLOW_APISERVER=768m
# Holds the Spark driver and the dbt/DuckDB subprocess. Spark takes 4 GB of it.
MEM_AIRFLOW_SCHEDULER=6144m
MEM_AIRFLOW_DAGPROC=512m
MEM_OPS=128m
SPARK_DRIVER_MEMORY=4g
SPARK_SHUFFLE_PARTITIONS=64
GEN_EVENT_COUNT=500000
